  "asked": "# Build: handoff-2-addenda (Fable for the credential/role/protocol steps, Opus for UI) **Name:** Handoff 2 add-ons · **Category:** Plugin extension (session-sync) ## Why (Brett, voice, Nov 4 2026) Handoff 2 (build `handoff-2`, PR #338, plugin `session-sync`) finished BEFORE these addenda reached its session; the tmux nudges never landed. Brett: \"Okay, do it... put them all. Do that now.\" Base is branch `claude/handoff-2` (PR #338). Build on top of it. If #338 merges first, rebase onto main. Open your own PR that lands after #338 (merge queue only). ## What to add: the addenda at the END of `/root/axf-builds/handoff-2/.brief.md`, which #338 does NOT contain. Read them verbatim. Summary: 1. **Session chip under every model badge** (Build manager, Builds, queue views, Plan Studio, Git board, Home cards, API/MCP/CLI `session` field): **Main** or **Helper 2 / Helper 3...** (stable numbers per helper), tooltip with crew agent, account, since when, and Take back. 2. **Every helper runs on ITS OWN Claude subscription (Fable step)**: on /sync join, the helper registers a `claude setup-token` subscription token via a one-time pairing page on axHub (never in chat, repo, logs, store, sync files or screenshots), encrypted in axHub's secret store, shown masked with Revoke/Replace, expiry and a pre-expiry alert. Each account gets an isolated config dir on the VPS (`/root/.claude-accounts/<helper-id>/`, mode 700), and helper-owned jobs launch with that account only (CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR / CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN scoped to the process). **Never fall back to the main account**: missing/expired/rate-limited means the job waits with a badge + notification. Per-account usage on the badge. Verify on connect with a tiny test call showing the account email. Also a **multi-token manager** screen listing every connected account/token. 3. **Model access check + bounce**: Fable/any model CAN be sent to helpers. On receiving work, the helper verifies it can run every required model (real check, cached). If not, it auto-rejects just the steps it can't run, and they go back to the **helper desk**, which reassigns them to a free main-account crew agent that can run the model, keeping position. Helpers report model access on join (warning only, never a block on send). 4. **Brownie runs the helper desk, NOT Patches**: offering work, Request jobs, step splitting for helpers, bounces, reassignments, Take back, heartbeat/offline holds. Patches keeps the main queue only. Show 'Helper desk: Brownie' on badges/tooltips. Brownie keeps QA; add skill 'helper-desk' to her card. 5. **Every hop posted in the group chat** (Breakroom Sessions channel) as each actor: helper 'Rejected <step>: no Fable here, back to you @Brownie' -> Brownie 'Reassigning <step> to <agent> (Main, Fable)' -> agent 'Picked up <step>'. Badges update live through the hand-back. 6. **Brownie's attitude**: sassy whip-cracking floor boss (persona notes via claude_session_persona); light swearing OK, no slurs, nothing sexual, always informative (build/step, status, next action). Escalation timers (plain code): nudge at 2x the step estimate, whip-crack post at 3x, yank back + reassign + write-up line at 4x or a missed heartbeat. Sass level Mild/Spicy/Savage (default Spicy) and thresholds in Settings. ## Rules Fable for 2 + the role/protocol bits of 3-4; downgrade to Opus (allowed) for UI. Resumable steps (progress file ticked + pushed every step). Book to a free named agent. Create/tick a Plan Studio plan 'Handoff 2 add-ons'. Basic docs/README.md update, tests (incl. never-fall-back-to-main and token-never-logged tests), UI Review shots (non-blocking). PR **through the merge queue only**. Report in _claude/builds/reports/. Commits clean. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-